  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "The dry bulk sale and purchase market remained stable with asset values largely \nunaffected, despite a minor decline in the overall freight market. The Baltic Dry Index (BDI) fell to a \nmulti-week low on Monday, but rebounded over the week and closed today at 2743 points, more or less \nthe same level as last Friday (2752 points). Buyers are refusing to go on summer holidays, as \ndemonstrated by another busy week with 16 transactions recorded, comprising 2 capes, 1 post-\nPanamax, 1 kamsarmax, 1 panamax, 5 Ultramaxes, 3 Supramaxes & 3 Handysize bulk carriers.  \n \nWe have gathered from market insights that post-panamax PONT ROUGE (99,992 dwt blt \n2021/Tsuneishi Zhoushan P.R.C) is trading firm at region $ 36 million, while hearing scrubber fitted \nkamsarmax MONT FORT (82,113 dwt blt 2012/Tsuneishi Japan in under firm negos at region $ 22 \nmillion. We also picked up that Greek controlled supramax CAPT EUGENE (55,499 dwt blt \n2010/Mitsui, Japan is negotiating firm close to region of $16.6 million.  \n \nFor a detailed review and additional information regarding these week's transactions, kindly refer to \nour \"representative sales\" section.",
    "demolition": "The Subcontinent markets remain stable. Pakistan and Bangladesh continue to \ndemonstrate a strong and positive outlook, whereas India maintains stability but with a weaker forecast. \nFor an overview of demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
